l. All judoka losing to the winner of each pool advanced to repêchage pools, with the winners of the repêchage pools earning bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The 1981 and 1983 World Championships had been won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/34549"} "Yasuhiro Yamashita"] " (JPN), but he elected to compete only in the open class in Los Angeles. The 1983 open class World Champion had been the 145 kg. (329 lb.) " [:a {:href "/athletes/34313"} "Hitoshi Saito"] ", and he was the Japanese choice for this class. Saito won his early matches very easily, with three matches taking him only 90 seconds for three " [:em {} "ippons"] ". In the final, he faced the defending champion, France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/34206"} "Angelo Parisi"] ". Parisi had an unusual international record. He was European Champion in 1977, 1983, and 1984, but never placed at the World Championships. The final was a passive affair, with both fighters being warned for inactivity. Eventually Saito won a close match only by " [:em {} "shido"] " at the time limit. Parisi was Italian-born, but grew up a British citizen in England, and represented France by virtue of marrying a French woman."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34313"} "Hitoshi Saito"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34206"} "Angelo Parisi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {